[00:19.92]1. The greatest of men was our Lord Jesus Christ;
[00:27.12]By pride or ambition, he was not enticed.
[00:34.42]God’s purpose gave Jesus the prominent role;
[00:41.04]Yet, lowly in heart, he was always whole-souled.
[01:01.34]2. To all who are toiling with troublesome cares,
[01:08.68]He offers to carry the burdens they bear.
[01:15.90]Refreshment they find as the Kingdom they seek.
[01:22.42]With kindness and mildness, he favors the meek.
[01:38.42]3. ‘We all are just brothers,’ our Lord Jesus said.
[01:46.50]In humble submission, we look to our Head.
[01:53.04]The mild and the meek ones to God have great worth;
[02:00.10]He promises they will inherit the earth.
